(2) An independent cross-model reviewer assessed your work:
=== REVIEW ===
{{nodes.anchor_check.result.annotatedText}}
Any citation marked [UNVERIFIED CITATION: ...] could not be resolved against the tree — treat those with skepticism while weighing the finding on its merits. The review is ADVISORY: address every finding that is real (fix it), and for any finding you judge wrong, say WHY in one line (reviewer context is thinner than yours). Do not relitigate spec-pinned decisions the reviewer failed to notice were pinned.

If the gate is green AND the review APPROVED (or its findings are all non-issues): reply 'VERIFIED-GREEN' plus one line. Change nothing.
Otherwise: fix everything real (still confined to packages/experience-memory/, still no commits), then summarize what changed and why.

